.TH tkuwheel n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuwheel
.PP
Forward mouse\-wheel events to a scrollable target. Solves a common Tk problem: embedded windows (e.g. a frame inside a \fBtext\fR widget) and ordinary child widgets receive the wheel event themselves, so an outer scroller stops scrolling while the pointer is over them. \fBtkuwheel\fR re\-binds the wheel on a widget \-\- and, by default, its whole subtree \-\- so the events are sent to a target widget's \fByview\fR / \fBxview\fR. Pure Tk, Tcl/Tk 8.6+ / 9.x.
.PP
Cross\-platform: it binds \fB<MouseWheel>\fR (Windows/macOS) and \fB<Button\-4>\fR / \fB<Button\-5>\fR (X11). Direction comes from the sign of the delta, so one notch scrolls a fixed number of units regardless of the platform's delta magnitude.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkuwheel::redirect target w ?-orient y|x|both? ?-amount N? ?-recursive 0|1?
::tkutils::tkuwheel::unbind   w ?-recursive 0|1?
.CE
.SS redirect
.PP
Binds the wheel on \fBw\fR so the events scroll \fBtarget\fR. \fBtarget\fR must understand the standard \fByview\fR / \fBxview scroll N units\fR protocol (text, canvas, listbox, ttk::treeview, ...). Returns \fBw\fR.
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-orient y\fR	\fBy\fR	plain wheel scrolls \fBtarget\fR vertically
\fB\-orient x\fR		plain wheel scrolls \fBtarget\fR horizontally
\fB\-orient both\fR		plain wheel = vertical, \fBShift\fR+wheel = horizontal
\fB\-amount N\fR	\fB3\fR	units scrolled per wheel notch (positive integer)
\fB\-recursive\fR	\fB1\fR	bind every descendant of \fBw\fR too (\fB0\fR = only \fBw\fR)
.TE
.PP
The subtree is bound as it exists at call time; re\-run \fBredirect\fR after adding child widgets. Bindings are removed automatically when \fBw\fR is destroyed.
.SS unbind
.PP
Removes the wheel bindings that \fBredirect\fR set on \fBw\fR (and its subtree unless \fB\-recursive 0\fR).
.SS Example
.CS
package require tkutils::tkuwheel

# A frame full of labels embedded in a scrolling text widget would otherwise
# swallow the wheel. Forward it back to the text widget:
text .t -yscrollcommand {.sb set}
ttk::scrollbar .sb -command {.t yview}
grid .t .sb -sticky nsew

frame .t.card
label .t.card.title -text "Embedded"
label .t.card.body  -text "Scrolls the text widget anyway"
pack  .t.card.title .t.card.body
\&.t window create end -window .t.card

::tkutils::tkuwheel::redirect .t .t.card        ;# wheel over the card scrolls .t
.CE
.SS Errors
.PP
Error code \fB{TKUTILS TKUWHEEL <REASON>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
REASON	When
\fBOPTION\fR	unknown option, missing value, bad \fB\-orient\fR / \fB\-amount\fR / \fB\-recursive\fR
\fBWINDOW\fR	\fBtarget\fR or \fBw\fR does not exist
.TE
